sec.p:
We use a positive degree day (PDD) ice sheet surface mass balance model to estimate the atmospheric impacts of North Pacific meltwater on Laurentide and European ice sheets. This model assumes that melt is proportional to the sum of daily mean air temperature above 0 ˚ C (i.e., PDD). Because our model output data is at a monthly resolution, a normal distribution is assumed for daily temperature variations. For each month, the monthly mean PDDm (°C day) is calculated using the equation66:1\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
                                                  \usepackage{amsmath}
                                                  \usepackage{wasysym}
                                                  \usepackage{amsfonts}
                                                  \usepackage{amssymb}
                                                  \usepackage{amsbsy}
                                                  \usepackage{mathrsfs}
                                                  \usepackage{upgreek}
                                                  \setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
                                                  \begin{document}$${{{\rm{PDD}}}}_{m}={N}_{m}\cdot \frac{1}{\sigma \sqrt{2\pi }}{\int }_{\!\!\!\!0}^{\infty }T\cdot \exp \left(-\frac{{\left(T-{T}_{m}\right)}^{2}}{2{\sigma }^{2}}\right){dT}$$\end{document}PDDm=Nm⋅1σ2π∫0∞T⋅exp−T−Tm22σ2dTwhere Nm is the number of days in month m; Tm is the monthly mean surface temperature from our model output. σ is assumed to be 5 ˚C67. The equation can be solved using an error function following Calov and Greve68:2\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
                                                  \usepackage{amsmath}
                                                  \usepackage{wasysym}
                                                  \usepackage{amsfonts}
                                                  \usepackage{amssymb}
                                                  \usepackage{amsbsy}
                                                  \usepackage{mathrsfs}
                                                  \usepackage{upgreek}
                                                  \setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
                                                  \begin{document}$${{{\rm{PDD}}}}_{m}={N}_{m}\cdot \left[\frac{\sigma }{\sqrt{2\pi }}\exp \left(-\frac{{{T}_{m}}^{2}}{2{\sigma }^{2}}\right)+\frac{{T}_{m}}{2}{{\rm{erfc}}}\left(-\frac{{T}_{m}}{\sqrt{2}\sigma }\right)\right]$$\end{document}PDDm=Nm⋅σ2πexp−Tm22σ2+Tm2erfc−Tm2σ

Monthly surface mass balance, SMBm, is calculated as3\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
                                                  \usepackage{amsmath}
                                                  \usepackage{wasysym}
                                                  \usepackage{amsfonts}
                                                  \usepackage{amssymb}
                                                  \usepackage{amsbsy}
                                                  \usepackage{mathrsfs}
                                                  \usepackage{upgreek}
                                                  \setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
                                                  \begin{document}$${{{\rm{SMB}}}}_{m}={S}_{m}-{M}_{m}+{R}_{m}$$\end{document}SMBm=Sm−Mm+Rmwhere Sm is the monthly mean snowfall accumulation (mm/month) from our model output; Mm is monthly snow melt rate (mm/month), and Rm is the refreeze of melted snow (mm/month). Mm and Rm are calculated as:4\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
                                                  \usepackage{amsmath}
                                                  \usepackage{wasysym}
                                                  \usepackage{amsfonts}
                                                  \usepackage{amssymb}
                                                  \usepackage{amsbsy}
                                                  \usepackage{mathrsfs}
                                                  \usepackage{upgreek}
                                                  \setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
                                                  \begin{document}$${M}_{m}={D}_{{{\rm{snow}}}}\cdot {{{\rm{PDD}}}}_{m}$$\end{document}Mm=Dsnow⋅PDDm5\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
                                                  \usepackage{amsmath}
                                                  \usepackage{wasysym}
                                                  \usepackage{amsfonts}
                                                  \usepackage{amssymb}
                                                  \usepackage{amsbsy}
                                                  \usepackage{mathrsfs}
                                                  \usepackage{upgreek}
                                                  \setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
                                                  \begin{document}$${R}_{m}={f}_{{{\rm{refreeze}}}}\cdot {M}_{m}$$\end{document}Rm=frefreeze⋅Mmwhere Dsnow is a constant degree-day factor of 3 mm ˚C-1 day-1 66,67, and frefreeze is the refreezing factor, which is set as 0.5 in this study, commonly used for the Greenland Ice Sheet today66. The annual mean ice sheet mass balance is calculated as the sum of SMBm.
